.TH spin 1 "Oct 2026" "Beta:👣v5.0" "General Commands Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.
.SH NAME
spin \- animated spinner for command line with parallel command execution
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spin
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.B --cmd
.IR COMMAND [ , COMMAND ]...
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
spin is a command line (CLI) tool written in C++ that displays an animated spinner while a background process is running. It is useful for visually indicating that a task is in progress, especially if the task takes a considerable amount of time.
.
.PP
Commands passed to
.B --cmd
are separated by commas and executed in parallel, one shell per command, using up to the number of workers detected from the CPU cores and the system process limit. The exit status is 0 only if every command succeeded.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.
.SS General options:
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display help and exit
.TP
.B --version
Show version and exit
.TP
.B -t TEXT, --text=TEXT
Text to show next to the spinner
.TP
.B -i INT, --interval=INT
Frame interval in milliseconds (default: 100)
.TP
.B --style=NAME
Built-in spinner style name (see \fB--show-style\fR)
.TP
.B --frames=FRAMES
Custom frames, e.g. \fB"⠋⠙⠚"\fR or \fB"one,two,three"\fR
.TP
.B --position=POSITION
Spinner position: \fBbefore\fR (default) or \fBafter\fR the text
.TP
.B --text-style=STYLE
Text style: \fBnormal\fR, \fBbold\fR, \fBdim\fR, \fBitalic\fR, \fBunderline\fR or \fBreverse\fR
.TP
.B --cmd=COMMAND
Command to execute. Separate multiple commands with commas to run them in parallel
.TP
.B -c COLOR, --color=COLOR
ANSI 256 text color (0-255)
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Suppress command output (spinner and result messages included)
.
.SS Execution:
Parallel command execution
.TP
.B -j N, --jobs=N
Maximum number of parallel jobs. \fB0\fR (default) auto-detects from the online CPU cores bounded by the system process limit
.TP
.B --wake-threshold=N
Number of queued commands that take the Android wake lock. Values below 1 disable it (default: 3)
.TP
.B --no-wake-lock
Never take the Android wake lock, regardless of the queue length
.TP
.B --pin-workers
Pin each worker to its own CPU core (useful on big.LITTLE SoCs)
.TP
.B --log=PATH
Path of the execution log (default: \fI$HOME/.spin.log\fR, rotated at 1 MiB)
.
.SS Information:
Show available options and exit
.TP
.B --show-colors
Show the list of 256 ANSI colors
.TP
.B --show-style
Show the built-in spinner styles
.TP
.B --show-text-styles
Show the available text styles
.TP
.B --show-positions
Show the spinner positions
.TP
.B --show-system
Show the detected CPU topology (cores, process limit, safe workers, max frequencies)
.
.SS Result:
Display status after completion
.TP
.B --result
Display a message after execution finishes
.TP
.B -e TEXT, --error=TEXT
Custom message for the failure case
.TP
.B -s TEXT, --success=TEXT
Custom message for the success case
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All commands succeeded
.TP
.B 1
At least one command failed, or --cmd was missing/invalid options were given
.TP
.B 2
Option parse error
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.spin.log
Default execution log (one entry per command with timestamp, PID, exit code and status)
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show a spinner with custom text while sleeping:
.PP
.RS
spin -t "Loading.." -c 105 --cmd "sleep 2"
.RE
.PP
Run three commands in parallel with two workers:
.PP
.RS
spin -j 2 --cmd "sleep 10, sleep 15, sleep 20"
.RE
.PP
Install several packages, showing a result message:
.PP
.RS
spin --result --success "All installed" --cmd "pkg install -y git, pkg install -y curl"
.RE
.PP
Pin the workers and log to a custom file:
.PP
.RS
spin --pin-workers --log $HOME/build.log --cmd "make, make test"
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://victorh028.github.io/spin/
